 r←Test_POSTRefresh_PendingRuns url;Assert;Authed;before;state
⍝ Check a queued refresh actually runs once the current one finishes.
⍝ The only test here that does real refreshes, because real workers looping is the
⍝ property under test. Counts cycles rather than comparing started_at: ISODateTime has
⍝ 1s resolution, so two cycles inside the same second stamp identical timestamps.
 r←0
 Assert←##.Assert
 Authed←##.MAIN.Authed
 state←#.DCMS.GLOBAL.refresh
 :Trap 0
     'Refresh already running at start of test'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 150
     before←state.cycles
     'Expected 202 Accepted'Assert 202=('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run.HttpStatus
     'Expected 202 Accepted'Assert 202=('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run.HttpStatus
     'Refresh did not return to idle'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 600
    ⍝ Two triggers must produce two cycles, whether the second queued behind the first
    ⍝ or started its own once the first finished. Either way they were serialised.
     'Two triggers did not produce two refresh cycles'Assert 2≤state.cycles-before
     'Pending flag not cleared'Assert 0=state.pending
     r←1
 :EndTrap
⍝ Teardown: never leak a refresh worker into the next test
 {}##.WaitRefreshIdle 600
